{"entity": "DocBench", "type": "data", "description": "DocBench is a challenging multimodal Document Question Answering benchmark designed to evaluate model performance across varying document lengths and to validate the effectiveness of the RAG-Anything approach. It comprises 229 documents spanning five domains and document types, with an average length of 66 pages and approximately 46,377 tokens per document. The benchmark includes 1,102 expert-crafted question-answer pairs. Its documents encompass medium- to long-length materials across various domains, including legal, governmental, and financial files, with financial reports averaging 192 pages and news consisting of concise single-page newspapers; detailed statistics are provided in Table 5.\n\nDocBench serves as an evaluation dataset for the RAG-Anything framework and its variants, enabling sophisticated visual interpretation and evidence-grounded response generation. On this benchmark, RAG-Anything outperforms MM-GraphRAG by over 13 points on documents exceeding 100 pages, a performance gap that expands dramatically at that document length. Representative cases from DocBench have been analyzed to demonstrate how RAG-Anything leverages structural information and intra-modal structures."}
